* Ephemeral keys on Aztec
** Why a fresh key per message
*** Sender knows only an address
*** No linkable sender key in the ciphertext
*** Nothing durable protects the message
*** Ephemeral-static Diffie-Hellman
** Grumpkin, embedded in BN254
*** y^2 = x^3 - 17 over Fr
*** Scalars in Fq: EmbeddedCurveScalar {lo, hi}
*** Native arithmetic inside a circuit
*** Positive-y convention, x sent alone
** An address is a public key
*** address_point = pre_address * G + Ivpk_m
*** address = address_point.x
*** address secret = pre_address + ivsk
** One message, AES-128
*** S = eph_sk * address_point
*** s_app = Poseidon2(S, contract)
*** two key/IV pairs, body + header, CBC
*** 31-byte packing, masks, eph_pk.x first
*** random padding to 15 fields, no MAC
** Handshakes and tags
*** Non-interactive: 2nd eph key, S' = k * S
*** Announcement encrypted to the recipient
*** Interactive: eph key never published
*** Address-derived / arbitrary: no eph key
** Post-quantum?
*** ECDH on Grumpkin: Shor breaks it
*** Every onchain log carries eph_pk.x
*** Harvest now, decrypt later
*** Poseidon2 commitments hold (Grover)
*** Proof soundness, signatures: broken
*** Hybrid KEM: bigger log, KEM key in address, in-circuit cost
@endmindmap
